.TH NYX-PORTSCAN 8 "2025" "NYX Framework" "NYX Phobos Tools"
.SH NAME
nyx-portscan \- TCP port scanner
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nyx-portscan
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nyx-portscan
determines the state of TCP ports on a single target host:
.BR open ,
.BR closed ,
or
.BR filtered .
.PP
When launched, it enters an interactive shell with line editing,
tab completion, and command history. Type
.B help
for available commands.
.PP
Two scan modes are supported:
.TP
.B TCP Connect
Uses
.BR connect (2)
with non-blocking sockets. Does not require root privileges.
.TP
.B TCP SYN (half-open)
Sends raw SYN packets and analyses responses. Requires root.
Faster and stealthier than TCP Connect.
.PP
When SYN mode is requested but the tool is not running as root,
it automatically falls back to TCP Connect with a warning.
.PP
This is an atomic, single-purpose tool. It does NOT identify
services, grab banners, or fingerprint versions.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.BI scan " -t ip" " [-p range]" " [-P n]" " [-m mode]" " [-T n]" " [-w ms]" " [-o]"
Run TCP port scan. Options:
.RS
.TP
.BI \-t " ip" "\fR, \fP" \-\-target " ip"
Target IPv4 address (required).
.TP
.BI \-p " range" "\fR, \fP" \-\-ports " range"
Port range (e.g. 1\-1024 or 80). Mutually exclusive with \fB\-P\fR.
.TP
.BI \-P " n" "\fR, \fP" \-\-top\-ports " n"
Scan top \fIn\fR most common ports. Default 100.
.TP
.BI \-m " mode" "\fR, \fP" \-\-mode " mode"
Scan mode: \fBconnect\fR or \fBsyn\fR. Default is auto.
.TP
.BI \-T " n" "\fR, \fP" \-\-threads " n"
Number of scanning threads. Default is 16.
.TP
.BI \-w " ms" "\fR, \fP" \-\-timeout " ms"
Per-port timeout in milliseconds. Default is 2000.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-open\-only
Only display ports in the \fBopen\fR state.
.RE
.TP
.B help
Show available commands and usage.
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
nyx-portscan
portscan> scan -t 192.168.1.5
portscan> scan -t 192.168.1.5 -p 1-1024 -m syn
portscan> scan -t 10.0.0.1 -P 20 -o
portscan> exit
.fi
.SH NOTES
TCP SYN scan requires root privileges. Without root, the tool
automatically falls back to TCP Connect mode.
